   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**China is catching up with the US in research spending.** In 2023, China spent **2.58%** of its GDP on research and the US **3.45%**: China's share is 75% of the US level, up from 34% in 2000.\n\nThe dashboard also compares researchers per million people, where the US is still well ahead. Source: UIS, February 2026 release; indicators EXPGDP.TOT, RESDEN.INHAB.TFTE.",
